1
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,220
I understand how you feel.

2
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:17,480
But how do you know Reiko
was taken to Scotland?

3
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:18,798
Well, no,

4
00:00:18,848 --> 00:00:22,760
The kidnappers have made a new demand.

5
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:29,020
They want the ransom doubled and brought to
Hata Border Castle at noon tomorrow, sharp.

6
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:31,420
Damn, those cowards.

7
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:33,980
Those guys are truly unforgivable.

8
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,060
So I've made up my mind.

9
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:41,180
Whoever rescues Reiko will marry her.

10
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,440
Marry?

11
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,920
I think rescuing her will probably
be a matter of life and death.

12
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:50,540
But the man who can overcome that is
the one worthy of being Reiko's husband,

13
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:55,080
and I think I can entrust the future of
the Akimoto Group to him as my successor.

14
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:57,480
I want to save Reiko, but as for marriage...

15
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:01,100
What on earth do you have to complain about?

16
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,405
Reiko is beautiful,
and on top of that she has a 95,

17
00:01:03,455 --> 00:01:06,400
58, 90 figure. What a body!

18
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:09,820
Being able to marry
her alone is super lucky!

19
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:10,475
On top of that,

20
00:01:10,525 --> 00:01:14,120
he'd become the heir to
my 2 trillion yen fortune!

21
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:16,260
What? 2 trillion yen?

22
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:20,900
That's right! You finally understand!

23
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:24,600
Yes! From today, I'll call you Father!

24
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:28,600
Even though you used me
and the championship...

25
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,440
You're supposed to be marrying Reiko-san.

26
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:38,840
When did you swear a future together?
First of all, you're a man, aren't you?

27
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:45,340
Hah, Nakagawa-kun,
I want you to rescue Reiko.

28
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:52,980
I'm counting on you. Hah, marriage aside,
I will definitely rescue Reiko-san.

29
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:58,700
Hatterborder Castle is a historic
castle built in the 15th century,

30
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:02,720
which has never once fallen into
enemy hands through many battles.

31
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:05,280
It is said to be an impregnable castle.

32
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:06,840
Here it comes at last.

33
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:08,220
That is...

34
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,900
So those guys already got here?

35
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,680
You dummy, Ban-chan.

36
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:15,360
What?

37
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,820
Chief, without a helicopter,
this'll be tough.

38
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:20,820
It's a huge castle.

39
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:24,020
You'd better do your best.

40
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:27,120
This music again...

41
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,660
A forced assault operation

42
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:33,500
Senpai, this way...

43
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:33,760
What?

44
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:36,660
It's Colonel Kepel's GSG9 helicopter.

45
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:40,300
What?

46
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,380
No way, the Nieser just collapsed!

47
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:51,380
Did you see that?

48
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:53,860
Behold the power of my border flag!

49
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:56,480
Doing their job.

50
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:01,660
Damn it, change of plans! Retreat!

51
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,560
If it comes to this, from the cliff below,
where the laser square is,

52
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,540
Who's calling at a time like this?

53
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:10,140
Honey, it's me.

54
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:10,960
Mom.

55
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:14,500
When are you finally going
to fix the bathroom plumbing?!

56
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:17,100
No, we're in the middle of an operation!

57
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:20,420
If you don't come home right now and fix it,
it's divorce!

58
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:21,300
Divorce.

59
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:23,440
Operation's over.

60
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:29,840
Aaaah! If we pull back the
fearless back-flip maneuver,

61
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:33,240
you lot will get shot
down and run home too, huh~

62
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:38,780
Whaaat? After coming all this way,
you can't just do that!

63
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:43,520
Nakagawa, landing.
Our button's on four. Roger.

64
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:54,040
There's no way we can escape from here.

65
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:03,840
Miss

66
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:06,000
It's time for your meal.

67
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,260
Excuse me.

68
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:20,740
They even bring our meals properly,

69
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,880
you're awfully kind for hostage-takers.

70
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,060
Who on earth are you people?

71
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:27,100
I'm afraid I can't say that.

72
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:30,220
I can guarantee only that
your life is safe, Miss,

73
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:31,880
so please rest assured.

74
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,660
Excuse me.

75
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,100
Something's definitely off.

76
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:45,540
For kidnappers, they're far too nice.

77
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:46,960
Let's go!

78
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:05,020
Damn it!

79
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:05,760
What?!

80
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:09,220
Ryotsu and Kankichi's men have
started climbing the cliff!

81
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,240
What?!

82
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:11,840
Don't let them catch up no matter what!

83
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:12,660
Let's go!

84
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:21,980
Chairman,
I've brought the young lady her meal.

85
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:26,180
Stop calling me chairman. I'm Mr. X.

86
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:29,200
My apologies, Mr. X.

87
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:32,040
So, how was Reiko-chan doing?

88
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:36,080
Well, she seems a bit out of sorts,
but she's fine.

89
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:39,400
Out of sorts Well, it can't be helped.

90
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:41,055
Mr. X,

91
00:05:41,105 --> 00:05:44,540
Colonel Kepel's GSG9 has
started climbing the cliff.

92
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:48,280
What happened to Colonel
Bakryu's Green Berets?

93
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:50,400
Looks like they've fully retreated.

94
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:52,140
That was surprisingly anticlimactic.

95
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:56,720
By the way,
is there any man who might meet my approval?

96
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:57,360
Yes.

97
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:01,140
I already know the Nakagawa Konzern's records,
so that's fine.

98
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:01,760
Then.

99
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:06,700
Well, among those peculiar Eastern constitutional...
no, among those strange ones in that Oriental lineup,

100
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,380
is there a man worth looking at?

101
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:13,720
The second son of the president of Yoshikawa Forestry,
known as the Forest King of Hokkaido.

102
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:14,960
That's Mamoru Yoshikawa.

103
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:18,780
I've met the president.
He's a very wealthy man.

104
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:20,700
Among the GSG9 as well,

105
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:23,440
is the son of the number
two man in the Omura zaibatsu.

106
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:25,460
there's Gerd Ebenbach.

107
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:29,960
Good. Leave only those three,
including Nakagawa-kun,

108
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,060
and take out the rest.

109
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:32,120
Understood.

110
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,040
Number 15, number 17 nozzle, perfume.

111
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:54,920
What is this visa?

112
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:06,720
It's a mat.

113
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:11,320
What's going on?

114
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,660
Good work, everyone.

115
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:14,440
Here you go.

116
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,000
What's this?

117
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,060
These are cell phone
straps for three locations.

118
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:21,080
There's one for each of you.

119
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:22,900
Hey, Yoshida.

120
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:25,760
Why is only you getting splashed with water?

121
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,320
I don't know either.

122
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,520
What is this for?

123
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,260
Take a look at the bookshelf store.

124
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,100
This one.

125
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,380
Bakryu.

126
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,800
As expected of the sauce.

127
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:44,480
Aaaaaaah!

128
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:47,080
Aaaaaaah!

129
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,560
Aaaaaaah!

130
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,720
Aaaaaaah!

131
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,320
Aaaaaaah!

132
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:53,680
Aaaaaaah!

133
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:56,080
Aaaaaaah!

134
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,460
Aaaaaaah!

135
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:57,580
Aaaaaaah!

136
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:57,640
Aaaaaaah!

137
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:57,680
Aaaaaaah!

138
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:02,240
Thanks for your hard work,
here's your participation prize.

139
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:06,040
Everyone.

140
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,440
Senpai, I can't go on anymore.

141
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:17,760
Hang in there, Honda, but don't push yourself too hard.
It's fine if you fall, but don't you dare die!

142
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,940
That's too hard, man.

143
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:28,160
Nakagawa, yours is the only one without water.
Don't worry about us, you climb up fast.

144
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:29,620
But!

145
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,284
Idiot! This plan is, you see,

146
00:08:31,334 --> 00:08:34,080
all that matters is saving Reiko!

147
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:35,840
Senpai...

148
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,740
Understood!

149
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:44,120
Alright! Let's go, Nakagawa!

150
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:47,680
Reiko...

151
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:50,560
Ryo-chan, here, have this if you like.

152
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:56,200
You've been eating nothing but cup ramen every day lately,
haven't you?

153
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:59,160
An unbalanced diet will make you sick.

154
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:00,620
Here, eat.

155
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,040
Thank you for the food.

156
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:07,520
This is good.

157
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:11,900
Sorry, please, Reiko.

158
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:14,620
Payday's still days away
and I don't have a single yen.

159
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:16,460
I can't even afford cup ramen.

160
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:20,460
Ten thousand yen... no, even a thousand is fine.
Please, lend me some.

161
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,160
Don't tell the Chief, okay?

162
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:26,020
Here you go.

163
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:28,820
R-Reiko...

164
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:34,660
So this is it, then.

165
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:46,260
Senpai, is everyone alright?

166
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:51,040
Nakagawa, did you cut off the water?

167
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:54,000
Yes, please hurry up and climb!

168
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:57,520
Alright, everyone, let's go rescue Reiko!

169
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:58,260
Yes!

170
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:03,520
As expected of the
Japanese police's teamwork!

171
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,060
No one dropped out?

172
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:08,980
But we've ended up with quite a few useless people left behind,
haven't we.

173
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:12,340
Let's pull ourselves together
and try once more here.

174
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:20,240
The path splits into five ways!

175
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:24,240
Ha ha Gentlemen,
you've managed to make it all the way here.

176
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,420
I'll give you credit for that.

177
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,220
Whoa! Who are you?

178
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:30,920
I'm Mr. X, the boss of Ryukai-dono.

179
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:33,140
What? Damn it!

180
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:35,000
Where did you put the Lego?

181
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:37,520
Whoa! Damn it!

182
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,120
W-what the...?

183
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:42,180
Senpai, it's a 3D projection!

184
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:44,700
What?! Damn it!

185
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:46,960
Pulling such a cornball stunt.

186
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:49,600
Ha ha Don't get so worked up.

187
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:53,560
A tough barrier is waiting for you ahead.

188
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:57,260
First, you'll split
into the pairs we assign.

189
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,500
Bear pair.

190
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,700
Rabbit pair.

191
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:03,620
Panda pair.

192
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,480
Elephant pair.

193
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:07,280
Gorilla pair.

194
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:11,560
Why do we have to be paired
up like kindergarteners?

195
00:11:15,060 --> 00:11:16,680
No questions allowed.

196
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:19,660
Now, choose whichever entrance you like.

197
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:22,400
Only two entrances can be passed through.

198
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:24,780
The other three have
obstacles prepared for them.

199
00:11:24,780 --> 00:11:26,860
Cowards will never make it through.

200
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:28,520
If you flinch, you're out.

201
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:30,580
Then, good luck to you.

202
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:32,480
Alright, Honda, let's go.

203
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,280
Yes.

204
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:42,800
It's a confetti ball!

205
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:47,640
A winner?

206
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:49,720
Nakagawa, you're so lucky!

207
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:52,960
We're the winners.

208
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,740
If it's a miss,

209
00:11:59,740 --> 00:12:01,020
what does that mean?

210
00:12:10,380 --> 00:12:11,740
Thanks for your hard work.

211
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:13,880
Here's your participation prize,
a cell phone strap.

212
00:12:16,620 --> 00:12:17,900
What's this "challenge" thing?

213
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:18,680
Come on now.

214
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:24,900
The two who drew the challenge cards will
now face the obstacles we've prepared.

215
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:26,220
What?

216
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:28,140
What exactly are these obstacles?

217
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:46,780
Come on. If you want to move forward,
you'll have to fight and defeat those lions.

218
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:49,940
Cowards won't survive.

219
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:15,220
Surprised, aren't you?

220
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:17,980
The lion and the wall were both holograms!

221
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:19,420
That's dirty!

222
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:21,740
Using such a cheap fake video!

223
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:26,740
I was supposed to have shown you I'd
use holograms by noon at the start.

224
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:30,000
It's your own fault for not noticing.

225
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,160
Damn it!

226
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:39,500
What's with this "challenge"?

227
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:48,940
Aaaaah! Yikes, eek eek eek eek!

228
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:58,440
Looks like we picked the worst entrance There's no way we can get through this!
Senpai, let's give up and run away!

229
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:11,640
Shut up! We've come this far, we can't give up! Wait...
this is a hologram! Yes, the hint was what he showed us earlier in the hall.

230
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,420
Falling for a trap like this...

231
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:20,720
No, it was the real thing!

232
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:32,100
It's a dead end!

233
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:34,100
Oh no, oh no!

234
00:14:37,740 --> 00:14:40,080
Senpai, what do we do?

235
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:42,940
I've brought something good.

236
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,180
What are you planning to do?

237
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,220
What do you think?

238
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:49,800
It's a pocket bike!

239
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:51,460
Come on, Honda, get on.

240
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:57,640
Calm as ever, my friend.

241
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,020
Seriously, you're not getting on?

242
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:01,920
Fine, I'll hold on tight.

243
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,400
You dinosaur!

244
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:05,360
Take this!

245
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:13,360
Yes! How about that, Mr. X!

246
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:18,520
Not bad.
But how will you handle the next stage?

247
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:20,620
You guys!

248
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,540
Senpai!

249
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,320
You guys!

250
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,600
Lord Ryo, I'm so glad you're safe!

251
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:29,300
Bringing Honda along was worth it.

252
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:30,740
I was so scared.

253
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:33,760
By the way, what are you guys doing here?

254
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,140
We're doing a quiz.

255
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:37,580
A quiz?

256
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:39,860
Save Reiko-chan!

257
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:41,560
Quiz Grand Prix!

258
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:45,360
From here on,
you'll compete in intelligence.

259
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:47,020
The top two will advance.

260
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:48,680
Don't mess with us!

261
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:50,240
Why a quiz, anyway?

262
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,000
And the material is way too old.

263
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,640
Can't you at least make it
Who Wants to Be a Millionaire?

264
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:57,540
Don't shout out the answers.

265
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:58,760
Then, first,

266
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:00,160
literature and history, Question 10.

267
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:01,860
Question.

268
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:03,680
Speaking of the three
great waka anthologies,

269
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:07,160
Kokinshū and one more. What's the other?

270
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:09,160
Man'yōshū.

271
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:13,780
This will weed out the idiots.

272
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:20,140
I've come to clear the dishes.

273
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:22,660
He's not here.

274
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,340
Sorry.

275
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:33,920
That's settled!

276
00:16:34,680 --> 00:16:38,120
Yes! Then next is 30 points
for Entertainment Music!

277
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:41,100
Who were the members of the
first-generation Rika-chan Trio?

278
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,060
Rika, Izumi, Wataru!

279
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:46,620
What kind of question is this?

280
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:49,540
I was told it would be a
really difficult question, so

281
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:56,360
No good! At this rate,
Leos will be left behind! End it!

282
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:58,420
End it!

283
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:01,700
Hey, hey, don't end it all of a sudden!

284
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:03,820
When the bell rings,
it's the final question, right?

285
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:05,060
That's right.

286
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:06,800
You, be quiet.

287
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,660
Well, fine.

288
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:11,240
Ryotsu's favorite,
Entertainment Music, is gone now.

289
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:14,020
Then, 30 points for the Non-Section.

290
00:17:15,140 --> 00:17:17,300
So, Buta-Gorira's real name is

291
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,240
Kumada Kaoru.

292
00:17:19,780 --> 00:17:21,500
Yet advances to the next round!

293
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:24,220
Ryotsu and his team were left behind.

294
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:26,780
What's a
"pig gorilla" supposed to be, anyway?

295
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:32,940
Did he really say that?
Nakagawa's team, Ryumei, advances!

296
00:17:32,940 --> 00:17:35,880
Yes! Ryo-sama is truly amazing!

297
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:39,140
Now, come on to the next stage. Yes.

298
00:17:39,140 --> 00:17:42,520
Senpai, do your best! Leave it to me.

299
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:48,140
This place is...

300
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:53,460
You two made it all the way here.
I'll give you credit.

301
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:57,840
Reiko Akimoto is up the stairs behind you.
You can reach her by climbing them.

302
00:17:58,420 --> 00:17:58,640
What?

303
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:00,240
Reiko!

304
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:01,080
Wait!

305
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:03,980
You!

306
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:06,340
The mokkori of the five
senses isn't for show!

307
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,580
When an incident happens on land,

308
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:11,400
one pair of swim trunks solves everything!

309
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,940
Leader of the Special
Crime Division Samba Lalas!

310
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:15,740
Swim-Trunks Deka!

311
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:18,740
Here I appear!

312
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,700
Why are you here!

313
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,460
As the final checkpoint,

314
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:25,000
you'll be fighting Swim-Trunks Deka and the

315
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,740
rest of the Special Crime Division.

316
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:30,960
That's how it is.

317
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:34,940
If you want to save the hostages,
you'll have to defeat me first.

318
00:18:34,940 --> 00:18:37,480
Why would a detective like
you side with the criminals?

319
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:40,180
I've wanted to fight you for ages,

320
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:43,380
I wanted to test which of us is stronger.

321
00:18:43,840 --> 00:18:44,980
That's the reason?

322
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:45,660
Senpai.

323
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:48,420
There seems to be something behind this.

324
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:50,480
Please let me go this time.

325
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,540
Fine.

326
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:55,180
Shall we begin?

327
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:56,820
Wait, Nakagawa.

328
00:18:58,420 --> 00:18:59,980
Have you forgotten the rules?

329
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:04,480
Here we go again.

330
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:06,900
Aaaaaah!

331
00:19:11,220 --> 00:19:17,360
Strip down, you! Me too.
Nakagawa, leave this one to me.

332
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:21,640
Ko-san was kidnapped at my shop. I'll do it.

333
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:23,940
Aaaaaah!

334
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:28,580
How about it?

335
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:30,320
You're naive, Nakagawa.

336
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:34,360
If you're hiding things like that,
you'll never beat me!

337
00:19:35,110 --> 00:19:37,540
Understood.

338
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:44,100
Good. That's what a man should be.

339
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:46,520
I'm Kei Yasuda of Moomus.

340
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:48,660
Spear thrust!

341
00:19:58,180 --> 00:19:58,980
Senpai

342
00:19:59,860 --> 00:20:02,620
P-please look after Reiko-san.

343
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:05,040
H-hey!

344
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:08,620
What's the point of defeating Nakagawa?

345
00:20:09,300 --> 00:20:11,000
If Kankichi Ryotsu wins

346
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,100
and Reiko's engagement is voided,

347
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,600
then the Akimoto Group is finished!

348
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:17,780
So that's what it was.

349
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:20,620
Just as I thought, Daddy.

350
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,020
To put on such a farce...

351
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:24,860
Reiko, is that you?

352
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:27,060
Ryo-chan, I'm so sorry!

353
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:30,380
Everything that happened this
time was to force me into marriage.

354
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:32,420
My daddy arranged all of it.

355
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:32,740
What?

356
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:37,300
I just said that if there was a
strong man who could protect me,

357
00:20:37,300 --> 00:20:39,240
I'd be willing to marry him.

358
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,600
Such a ridiculous thing!

359
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:43,180
So please, stop fighting now.

360
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:45,160
No can do.

361
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,340
Ryo-chan!

362
00:20:47,380 --> 00:20:48,680
Stop it, let go!

363
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,160
What's wrong, Reiko?

364
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:52,400
Sorry, Reiko-chan.

365
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:54,720
Stop it, Daddy!

366
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:55,580
Reiko!

367
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:57,300
Ryo-chan!

368
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:58,343
Reiko!

369
00:20:58,393 --> 00:21:02,160
Through all this,
I've realized that I love you!

370
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:07,820
I will defeat the Kaigan Deka and rescue you,
no matter what!

371
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,720
Ryo-chan...

372
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:12,168
That's a lie!

373
00:21:12,218 --> 00:21:14,900
You only want my fortune anyway!

374
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:16,080
Hurry up and take her away!

375
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:19,400
Ryo-chan!

376
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:22,380
That's how it is, Kaigan Deka.

377
00:21:22,380 --> 00:21:24,660
Let's settle this with a straight-up fight!

378
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:29,920
Bring it on.

379
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:30,640
Let's go.

380
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,280
Damn it!

381
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,760
Even in combat, he's pro-level.

382
00:21:40,760 --> 00:21:42,320
At this rate, I'm going down.

383
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:44,860
Closed it.

384
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:50,340
Not yet, not yet!

385
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:55,020
No way.

386
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:57,220
I'm embarrassed.

387
00:21:58,100 --> 00:21:59,800
Give me back my tie!

388
00:22:00,860 --> 00:22:01,580
Tie!

389
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:03,700
So that's it, you!

390
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:05,800
You're not embarrassed about being bare-assed naked,
are you?

391
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:08,160
Without a tie,
you must be totally embarrassed

392
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,100
J-just like that!

393
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:12,560
What's wrong, Kaigan Deka?

394
00:22:12,560 --> 00:22:15,560
Looks like you can't continue the fight.

395
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:17,920
This tie is...

396
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,400
It's the same as underwear.

397
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:23,140
Hey, if you admit defeat,

398
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:24,920
I'll give this tie back to you.

399
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:27,800
Fine, I lose.

400
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:29,860
This match

401
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:30,640
is mine.

402
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:33,120
I'll leave the tie right here.

403
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:34,260
See ya!

404
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:36,680
Reigo!

405
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:38,480
I'm coming!

406
00:22:43,980 --> 00:22:45,300
What's with this hatch?

407
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:55,440
What's going on? What's going on?

408
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,940
I love the sea and defend justice!

409
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:07,780
Who summoned me? Poseidon!

410
00:23:07,780 --> 00:23:10,360
Stuffed in a drawer, it's Tansu Rinkon!

411
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:16,080
I am the Water Police Squad Captain!

412
00:23:16,080 --> 00:23:17,740
Dozaemon of the sea!

413
00:23:17,740 --> 00:23:20,480
Ochadera Yasugi, cut for the Trade Burg...

414
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:22,080
Dolphin!

415
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:26,280
As always, your introduction is too long!

416
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,520
Ryotsu!

417
00:23:27,520 --> 00:23:30,360
Now that I'm here, it's game over for you!

418
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:32,860
You're going to do dolphin tricks again,
aren't you?

419
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:35,760
Unfortunately,
the Dolphins are staying home today.

420
00:23:36,180 --> 00:23:37,740
Let me get straight to the point today.

421
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:40,460
Torpedo launch!

422
00:23:49,500 --> 00:23:52,280
Aaaaaaah!

423
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:54,520
Eeeeeeh!

424
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:01,460
Are you all right?

425
00:24:02,380 --> 00:24:04,940
Well, he's strong... over there

426
00:24:06,140 --> 00:24:07,660
Eeeeeeh!

427
00:24:07,660 --> 00:24:08,760
0

428
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:08,920
This is it!

429
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:10,560
Use that!

430
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:15,600
Reiko! I'm coming!

431
00:24:18,120 --> 00:24:19,200
Standby!

432
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:19,940
That's reckless!

433
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:21,720
Reiko!

434
00:24:31,620 --> 00:24:32,600
That's...

435
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:39,740
It's no mere dazzling transformation!

436
00:24:39,740 --> 00:24:41,660
Bathing my back in the energy of the moon,

437
00:24:41,660 --> 00:24:44,080
justice's steps tear through the darkness!

438
00:24:44,820 --> 00:24:47,200
Leave the cases of the sky to me!

439
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:50,280
Messenger from the moon, Gekko Deka!

440
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:52,120
Venus Deka, too, at your service!

441
00:24:52,940 --> 00:24:53,940
Gekko Deka!

442
00:24:53,940 --> 00:24:55,500
Reiko!

443
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:57,040
Ryo-chan!

444
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:02,520
At this rate, they'll reach the summit.

445
00:25:02,520 --> 00:25:03,460
Linus Deka!

446
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:05,240
No transformation today, then.

447
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,000
Understood.

448
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:07,740
Farewell, Otakamori!

449
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:08,840
Is that all right?

450
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:09,940
Is that all right?

451
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:15,560
Why is it a statue of Saigō?

452
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,220
If you drop something like that,

453
00:25:17,220 --> 00:25:19,100
Eiko-chan could get hurt too!

454
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:19,880
Stop it!

455
00:25:20,480 --> 00:25:20,880
Hey!

456
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,600
Get the lasers ready!

457
00:25:23,100 --> 00:25:23,300
Yes.

458
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:57,200
Something's up!

459
00:26:04,940 --> 00:26:06,500
Stop it, please, just stop!

460
00:26:09,060 --> 00:26:10,520
Ryo-chan!

461
00:26:12,220 --> 00:26:14,060
You came to save me.

462
00:26:14,060 --> 00:26:16,300
Yeah, I made you a promise.

463
00:26:16,300 --> 00:26:17,700
Ryo-chan...

464
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:19,220
Back off!

465
00:26:19,620 --> 00:26:20,120
Yes.

466
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:22,020
Take this!

467
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:35,740
Reiko-chan!

468
00:26:37,540 --> 00:26:38,500
Reiko!

469
00:26:41,740 --> 00:26:43,080
Reiko-chan.

470
00:26:43,080 --> 00:26:45,520
It's your fault, isn't it!

471
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:52,060
Ryo-sama!

472
00:26:52,500 --> 00:26:54,560
Super! Ryo-chan! Super!

473
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:55,200
Is he all right?

474
00:26:55,500 --> 00:26:56,600
Of course he is!

475
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:59,380
He's just knocked out from the shock!

476
00:27:00,220 --> 00:27:02,400
Thank goodness! I'm so relieved!

477
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:04,740
Ryo-sama, I'm glad you're safe too.

478
00:27:05,180 --> 00:27:07,044
Heh, now, as promised,

479
00:27:07,094 --> 00:27:09,880
I've got the two trillion
yen and Reiko both!

480
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:12,820
That's right, Reiko's old man.

481
00:27:14,020 --> 00:27:15,000
What did you just say?

482
00:27:16,140 --> 00:27:18,060
Reiko, you were awake?

483
00:27:18,260 --> 00:27:19,200
Fuhahaha!

484
00:27:19,700 --> 00:27:23,500
So the real goal was two trillion yen,
and I was just a side bonus.

485
00:27:23,500 --> 00:27:25,780
N-no...

486
00:27:28,820 --> 00:27:33,480
I was stupid to think, even for a moment,
that I could become Ryo-chan's bride.

487
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:34,560
It's a misunderstanding, I swear.

488
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:36,560
I really do care about you...

489
00:27:37,460 --> 00:27:40,000
Yeah, that's right,
you'd better give up on a guy like that.

490
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:41,020
Papa.

491
00:27:41,020 --> 00:27:41,400
Yes.

492
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:45,700
I'll have a long talk
with you later too, Papa.

493
00:27:45,700 --> 00:27:47,500
Yes, I'm sorry.

494
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:50,680
I'm so tired.

495
00:27:51,140 --> 00:27:53,320
Papa, I'm going back to Tokyo.

496
00:27:53,320 --> 00:27:55,280
Yeah, yeah, all right, all right.

497
00:27:55,660 --> 00:27:58,820
Hey, bring a helicopter
down to the courtyard.

498
00:27:59,040 --> 00:28:02,040
Hold on! I saved Reiko!

499
00:28:02,240 --> 00:28:04,040
Hand over the money like we agreed!

500
00:28:04,340 --> 00:28:05,325
Sorry about that.

501
00:28:05,375 --> 00:28:08,610
Well, since Reiko says she
doesn't want to get married,

502
00:28:08,660 --> 00:28:10,100
the whole deal is off.

503
00:28:10,300 --> 00:28:11,120
Don't mess with me!

504
00:28:12,460 --> 00:28:13,060
Both!

505
00:28:15,060 --> 00:28:18,080
I had you all wrong.
Doing all this just for money!

506
00:28:18,380 --> 00:28:20,340
Come on, that's not fair.

507
00:28:25,100 --> 00:28:28,000
Hey! Take me with you too!

508
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:31,340
No! You need to reflect on that a little!

509
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:33,060
It's a misunderstanding!

510
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:38,640
Damn it! Why does it always end like this?!

511
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:55,720
Na na na na na na

512
00:28:55,720 --> 00:29:01,300
To those who gamble foolishly on their looks

513
00:29:01,300 --> 00:29:04,480
I probably don't want to be like that

514
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:09,080
If you're blocking the road at the corner,

515
00:29:09,080 --> 00:29:11,400
the moon has run away

516
00:29:12,100 --> 00:29:15,140
because now isn't everything

517
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:19,620
don't get so worked up about it

518
00:29:19,620 --> 00:29:27,540
even if you tell a little lie or cheat a little,
sometimes you're helping someone

519
00:29:27,540 --> 00:29:31,088
Baby, do you know me?

520
00:29:31,138 --> 00:29:33,880
Toward tomorrow, a nice spirit

521
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:41,360
I won't rot,
I'll do what needs doing, a cute spirit

522
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:48,380
being hard to understand is
because you want to seem that way

523
00:29:48,900 --> 00:29:54,540
isn't it better than changing how you look?

524
00:29:56,100 --> 00:30:01,120
na na na na na na na na na na na na

